/**
 * THE PANTRY SHEETS
 *
 * The second round of ingredient art: 98 more raw ingredients and 24 more finished
 * products, each on its own sheet of 128 px cells in an 8-column grid, sliced by
 * index exactly as `ingredientSheet.ts` and `productSheet.ts` are. They are separate
 * pictures rather than more cells on those sheets because the grids differ (7
 * columns of 138 px, 8 columns of 160 px), and one sheet has one cell size.
 *
 * Both sheets carry alpha, like the product sheet: an ingredient here sits on
 * whatever it is drawn over (label stock, the dark room) with no plate of its own.
 *
 * ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING, as it is in the older sheets: entry N of an order is
 * cell N of its picture. Append to both, never insert. Each line below is one ROW
 * of the picture (eight cells), which makes a wrong cell easy to find: the
 * ingredient sheet is 13 rows with two cells on the last, the product sheet 3.
 *
 * None of these ids is on the older sheets, in `PRODUCT_ALIAS`, or matched by the
 * patterns `IngredientIcon` folds generated ids through, so the lookup order in
 * that component cannot change which picture an older id draws.
 *
 * Embedded as data URIs for the same reason as every other sheet: the page ships
 * as one file whose CSP blocks external images. Registered once each as a class
 * by `IngredientIcon`, never inlined per item.
 */
export const PANTRY_COLS = 8;
export const PANTRY_CELL = 128;

